		{
			"date": "2023-12-10T13:26:18-08:00",
			"message": "sprites: make hatchling/octoball explosions snappier. (#1220)\nSomething that's bothered me for a while now: the hatchling dies, it slowly oozes blood and crumples, the fireball explosion sound plays in the middle of all that bleeding and crumpling, then it slow-motion explodes in total silence.\r\nPart of this the problem with the way the lost soul death is hard-coded - 6 tics per frame is just way too long for any decently snappy explosion. At best we can have like 2 actual \"exploding\" frames and the rest is just the bits floating in midair slowly fading away.\r\nThis PR skips the bleeding frames entirely in favour of what looks like a failed attempt at getting in one last attack, then a quick explosion right on the A_Scream frame followed by a few frames of that ring of glowing gore bits fading into nothing.\r\nA similar issue to the hatchling death animation exists with the octaminator projectile as well. The lines coming out of the current B frame still imply an explosion rather than a lingering cloud of debris.",
			"source": "freedoom",
			"url": "https://github.com/freedoom/freedoom/commit/54e555bc89ac4cda89ae88d28228c107be22142f",
			"sha": "54e555bc89ac4cda89ae88d28228c107be22142f",
			"contributions": [
				{
					"contributorId": "mc776",
					"relation": "Committer (updated animation timing for Skulk death explosion)"
				}
			],
			"index": 0,
